33adaf9d9d0c5eb2767e5ab48ca6b9a31b159a" commit="312b2ed95cca1b9935d1ab91b5afde15c116aeaf" commit_message="dut: Add Sphinx type hints for DUT components.  Some edit plugins like Jedi (or YouCompleteMe which also uses Jedi) can help development by providing auto completion. The DUT API, due to how it creates the instance, cannot be statically parsed to get right information.  The solution is to provide type information in docstring. Currently Jedi supports Sphinx doc (which we are already using) so we want to add the type information without changing all existing docstring format.  DUTBoard (via dut.Create()) and DUTComponent are the major classes we need to use, so the first change adds types to these two classes.  BUG=none TEST=make doc; make test  Change-Id: I8433adaf9d9d0c5eb2767e5ab48ca6b9a31b159a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/322910 Commit-Ready: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="322910" owner_email="hungte@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/10/322910/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="7849.0.0-rc1"/></manifest>